Lagos maybe a toy but it's not really  for kids you'll need a driver's license  to play with this creation this is the  world's first working car made almost  entirely from Legos more than a half a  million pieces were used and that's  1,100 pounds of plastic flaps  I have made some pretty cool Lego models  in my time but nothing as awesome as  this over five million people online  watch this clip of the cars maiden  voyage it's the work of Steve Sammartino  and Raoul Reuter who tore up the  instruction manual and became master  builder  took a trip down under to meet Steve  asked about the inspiration for such an  awesome project well it came from an  idea with RAL who I did it with he saw a  tiny Lego engine on YouTube and he  convinced me that he could build a giant  one so the project took 12 months in  building and about six months in  planning the build the car was built in  Romania and then we shipped the car to  Australia a lot of it fell apart in that  transporting process and then we've  rebuilt it here in Australia and did all  the test driving and filming of it  comfort is not one of its strong points  the steering wheel is very comfortable  to hold the seats are horrible it's a  bit of a bumpy ride but hey it's not  every day you can drive a car down the  road that's actually made of Lego it is  a huge achievement but the best part is  if they get bored with the car they  could always just build something else
 

